[description]

[b]Pull requests[/b] on Gitea mirror the familiar forge pattern: diff against base, threaded discussion, assignees, labels, and merge when checks pass. [b]Protected branches[/b] can require pull requests, disallow force-push, and require status checks—configuration depth varies by version, so read your release notes.

[b]Reviews:[/b] comment on lines or whole files; approve or request changes depending on UI support in your version. Smaller PRs still beat giant blobs for latency and reviewer fatigue.

[b]Draft / WIP:[/b] mark incomplete work so CI can run without implying merge readiness—naming conventions ([code]WIP:[/code] prefix) still appear in older instances.

[b]Takeaway:[/b] collaboration on Gitea is intentionally simpler than mega-suite products—use webhooks and external tools when you outgrow built-in policy.
